From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 15:57:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] v4l2codecs: av1: Keep the pool on downstream renegotiation

The AV1 decoder allocates the same way as the VP9 one: a downstream
reconfiguration while streaming runs decide_allocation() again through
the "Ignore downstream renegotiation request" path of negotiate(), and
a second set of OUTPUT and CAPTURE buffers is created next to the one
in the streaming queues, up to the VB2 limit of 32 buffers.

Keep the current allocation while streaming as long as the allocators
are in place. negotiate() resets the allocation on a format change, so
inter-frame resolution changes still get new buffers. The check was
dropped with commit 7fb19b37d8 ("v4l2codecs: av1: Allow inter-frames
resolution change").

Link: https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/gstreamer/gstreamer/-/merge_requests/13069
---
 sys/v4l2codecs/gstv4l2codecav1dec.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

--- a/sys/v4l2codecs/gstv4l2codecav1dec.c
+++ b/sys/v4l2codecs/gstv4l2codecav1dec.c
@@ -414,6 +414,10 @@ gst_v4l2_codec_av1_dec_decide_allocation
   guint min = 0, num_bitstream;
   gboolean has_videometa;
 
+  /* negotiate() only resets the allocation on a format change */
+  if (self->streaming && self->src_allocator)
+    goto no_internal_changes;
+
   g_clear_object (&self->src_pool);
   g_clear_object (&self->src_allocator);
   g_clear_object (&self->sink_allocator);
@@ -483,6 +487,7 @@ gst_v4l2_codec_av1_dec_decide_allocation
   self->src_pool =
       gst_v4l2_codec_pool_new (self->src_allocator, &self->vinfo_drm);
 
+no_internal_changes:
   /* Our buffer pool is internal, we will let the base class create a video
    * pool, and use it if we are running out of buffers or if downstream does
    * not support GstVideoMeta */
